Phase 1: Database & Architecture
The foundation of your application. All data relationships are established here.

Define User Schema: Map out members, their roles (Bureau, Subscriber), and authentication details.

Define Project Schema: Track project lifecycle, budgets, and committee assignments.

Define Financial Schema: Create the ledger for subscriptions, donations, and expenses linked to users and projects.

Initialize Database: Write and execute the SQL CREATE TABLE scripts in SQLite.

Map Foreign Keys: Ensure every transaction securely links back to a specific user and project.

Phase 2: Backend & Security
The brain of your application. Handles business logic and secures data access.

Initialize Server: Set up the Node.js and Express environment.

Implement Authentication: Integrate JSON Web Tokens (JWT) for secure user login.

Configure Access Control: Write middleware to ensure only Bureau members can edit financial data.

Build CRUD Endpoints: Develop API routes for managing users, projects, and transactions.

Configure File Storage: Set up multer to securely save uploaded receipts and CIN scans to a local directory.

Phase 3: Frontend & UI
The face of your application. Where users interact with the system.

Set Up React: Initialize the project and configure a routing system.

Build Dashboards: Create separate UI views for standard subscribers and Bureau administrators.

Develop Forms: Use react-hook-form to capture transaction details and project updates.

Integrate API: Connect the React frontend to your Express backend using fetch or axios.

Implement Visuals: Use charting libraries to display budget vs. expense progress visually.

Phase 4: Advanced Features
The professional touches that automate manual administrative work.

Integrate OCR Module: Connect Tesseract.js to scan CIN images and auto-fill registration inputs.

Set Up Email Automation: Configure Nodemailer with node-cron to send monthly payment reminders.

Build PDF Generator: Use jspdf to convert financial tables into printable reports for the General Assembly.

Create Audit Interface: Build a specific view for the Treasurer to cross-reference system transactions with bank statements.

Phase 5: Testing & Deployment
The final polish to ensure reliability and make the system live.

Conduct Financial Testing: Verify that all subscription and expense calculations are highly accurate.

Secure File Access: Ensure the uploads folder containing sensitive documents is restricted and not publicly accessible.

Configure VPS Server: Provision a Linux server for hosting.

Deploy Backend: Use PM2 to run the Express API continuously in the background.

Deploy Frontend: Build the React app and serve it using Nginx as a reverse proxy.